<%#
  The slot inside the engine's newsletter-success card
  (studio/profiles/_newsletter_modals, success_card partial:), rendered by
  NewsletterModalHelper. The card's props are the subscribe endpoint's JSON
  answer, in scope here as `props`. This is the product half of the beat; the
  card around it is the engine's.

  THE SEEDS BAR IS FIRST-JOIN ONLY. A re-subscribe earns nothing, so the bar is
  hidden rather than showing a flat zero. It self-heals from the seedsNavbar
  cache the seeds StateFanout just bumped (shared/_alpine_factories, the
  newsletter-state-changed listener).

  THE CTA IS SERVER-DECIDED. With the username quest still open (next_quest is
  :username) it swaps straight into the username card; otherwise it sends the
  player to browse contests. The engine card adds the Close link under it.
%>
<template x-if="(props.seeds_earned || 0) > 0">
  <div class="mb-5">
    <%= render "components/seeds_bar", seeds_data: display_seeds_data, compact: false %>
  </div>
</template>
<% if current_user.next_quest == :username %>
  <button type="button" @click="$store.modals.swap('username')" class="btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full">
    Next Quest
  </button>
<% else %>
  <%= link_to "Check Out Contests", contests_path,
              class: "btn btn-primary btn-lg w-full", "@click": "$store.modals.close()" %>
<% end %>
